# Architecture overview

> Human-owned project map. Record actual project-level structure and reading entries under the architecture convention; generated reference facts do not define architecture authority.

## Modules and responsibility

| Module | Main location / reading entry | Responsibility | Owning boundary | Why this boundary exists |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

Link an existing module README when it already provides useful navigation. Point to the actual startup/composition boundary and persistent state owners when they help explain how the project fits together; do not invent missing layers.

Use `docs/game-organization.md` to explain logic, presentation and their actual collaboration within these modules. Link relevant GDD, UI or game-presentation sources; do not split the map into fixed layer directories or treat development tools as gameplay responsibilities.

Briefly explain the problem each material boundary choice solves; link local implementation rationale to its Feature design and qualifying cross-Feature rationale to its ADR. Do not copy full plans, invent missing decision history or create an ADR just to supply a link.

## Allowed dependency directions

Describe the permitted directions between project-level modules and the reason for each constraint. Distinguish these constraints from key actual collaborations and their purpose. Record deliberate exceptions and their owner. Do not require a full class-level graph.

## Subsystem contracts

Link each documented subsystem's internal contracts at `architecture/<subsystem>.md`, using its stable name from the module list. Keep the overview at project level; explanation length and complexity do not select the location. Do not create empty subsystem files.

## Important decisions

Link relevant `architecture/adr-NNNN-<slug>.md` records when they exist. Keep tradeoffs and decision status in each ADR; this map describes the current structure. Omit this section when no ADR is needed.

## Standalone technical decisions

Use this section only for adopted decisions without a Feature that do not meet the ADR conditions and have project-level or cross-subsystem scope. Follow **Standalone technical decisions** in `methodology/10-architecture-overview.md`, including its fixed scope, authorization and migration rules. Keep decision rationale separate from actual implemented facts; omit the section when no matching content exists.

## Extracted facts

Optional generated facts live separately under `reports/maintenance/architecture-facts/`. Label extractor, source snapshot, scope and limitations. Explicit resource, path or type references are evidence of references, not proof of allowed dependencies, runtime ownership or architectural intent.

## Maintenance

Follow the Navigation and Maintaining a map sections of `methodology/10-architecture-overview.md` for content, change triggers and checks. Resolve conflicts with Product, Project Rules and approved decisions; do not silently replace human intent with generated output.
